WEBVTT

00:00:00.597 --> 00:00:01.390
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.689 --> 00:00:04.190
This lesson is for everyone who works in beauty:

00:00:04.298 --> 00:00:07.310
nails, lashes, hair or spa.

00:00:07.814 --> 00:00:10.709
However skilled you are, if your tools are not clean,

00:00:10.659 --> 00:00:13.070
a client can still end up with an infection.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:15.372
Today I'll show you the complete,

00:00:15.322 --> 00:00:18.510
correct routine for handling your tools after every client.

00:00:19.123 --> 00:00:25.249
Bacteria, fungi and viruses, such as the hepatitis viruses, spread in three ways:

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.169
through tools, through the hands of the technician, and through surfaces.

00:00:29.758 --> 00:00:33.696
The risk is highest when a tool touches scratched or broken skin,

00:00:33.646 --> 00:00:35.969
or a mucous membrane, such as the eye.

00:00:36.594 --> 00:00:39.585
There are three levels, and you need to tell them apart clearly.

00:00:39.913 --> 00:00:41.265
Level one is cleaning:

00:00:41.493 --> 00:00:44.624
washing the dirt away with water, soap and a brush.

00:00:45.057 --> 00:00:47.025
Level two is disinfection:

00:00:47.324 --> 00:00:52.065
it reduces the number of microorganisms to a safe level, but may not kill spores.

00:00:52.562 --> 00:00:54.545
Level three is sterilization:

00:00:54.818 --> 00:00:58.515
it kills all microorganisms, spores included, with heat,

00:00:58.465 --> 00:01:01.185
in an autoclave or a dry heat sterilizer.

00:01:01.819 --> 00:01:03.519
Which tools need which level?

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:08.420
Tools that touch the client, for example combs, scissors and lash tweezers,

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:11.999
must at least be cleaned and disinfected after every client.

00:01:12.508 --> 00:01:16.608
Tools that can pierce or cut the skin, or touch broken skin,

00:01:16.558 --> 00:01:19.039
for example cuticle nippers, blades,

00:01:19.069 --> 00:01:24.239
needles, comedone extractors, and pedicure tools, must be sterilized.

00:01:24.545 --> 00:01:29.376
And disposable items, like paper files, wooden sticks and lash wands,

00:01:29.326 --> 00:01:31.039
go in the bin after use.

00:01:31.596 --> 00:01:33.118
It all starts with your hands.

00:01:33.358 --> 00:01:38.062
Wash them with soap, dry them, then sanitize your hands before every client,

00:01:38.012 --> 00:01:39.838
and before putting on gloves.

00:01:40.347 --> 00:01:43.678
Gloves only protect you for a short time, so change them often.

00:01:44.209 --> 00:01:48.798
While you are wearing gloves, do not touch your phone, door handles or the lamp.

00:01:49.149 --> 00:01:51.198
If you do, put on a fresh pair.

00:01:51.866 --> 00:01:54.969
As soon as the client gets up, the first job is sorting.

00:01:55.228 --> 00:01:56.969
Disposable items go in the bin.

00:01:57.234 --> 00:02:01.609
Metal tools go into a separate tray for used items, never mixed with clean ones.

00:02:02.166 --> 00:02:02.973
Step one:

00:02:03.237 --> 00:02:03.853
cleaning.

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:06.351
Wearing gloves, open the tools fully,

00:02:06.301 --> 00:02:09.773
and scrub them well with a brush and soap under running water,

00:02:10.042 --> 00:02:11.773
especially the joints and grooves.

00:02:12.177 --> 00:02:15.293
Wash them right away, and never let the dirt dry on.

00:02:15.641 --> 00:02:20.360
This step can never be skipped, because dirt left behind shields the bacteria,

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.293
and makes disinfection and sterilization useless.

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:27.293
After washing, rinse with clean water, and dry them thoroughly.

00:02:27.961 --> 00:02:28.816
Step two:

00:02:28.992 --> 00:02:29.856
disinfection.

00:02:30.532 --> 00:02:33.936
Fully submerge the tools in a disinfectant made for instruments.

00:02:34.265 --> 00:02:38.719
Mix it at the right concentration, and leave them in for the full time on the label,

00:02:38.669 --> 00:02:39.296
never less.

00:02:39.931 --> 00:02:42.496
Change the solution as the manufacturer instructs.

00:02:42.669 --> 00:02:43.136
Note:

00:02:43.325 --> 00:02:46.736
a quick spray of alcohol and a wipe is not proper disinfection.

00:02:47.431 --> 00:02:48.337
Step three:

00:02:48.451 --> 00:02:51.377
sterilization, for the tools that can break the skin.

00:02:51.885 --> 00:02:55.967
Put the clean, dry tools into a sterilization pouch, seal it,

00:02:55.917 --> 00:02:58.017
then place it in the autoclave,

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:02.017
or the dry heat sterilizer, and run the correct program on the machine.

00:03:02.606 --> 00:03:07.217
The pouch usually has an indicator strip that changes color to show the cycle was successful.

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:08.097
Please note:

00:03:08.446 --> 00:03:12.897
a soaking solution advertised as sterilizing does not replace an autoclave.

00:03:13.543 --> 00:03:18.118
Write the date on sterilized pouches, and store them in a dry, clean,

00:03:18.068 --> 00:03:21.397
dust free place, separate from unsterilized items.

00:03:21.825 --> 00:03:24.677
Only open the pouch in front of the client, just as you begin.

00:03:25.226 --> 00:03:28.277
When clients see that, they feel reassured straight away.

00:03:28.876 --> 00:03:33.468
After every client, wipe down the table, the arm rest, the bed and the chair,

00:03:33.418 --> 00:03:37.243
then disinfect the surfaces that touched the skin of the client.

00:03:37.678 --> 00:03:40.923
Use fresh towels and a fresh paper liner for each person.

00:03:41.496 --> 00:03:42.614
For hair salons:

00:03:42.647 --> 00:03:45.014
use a disposable neck strip under the cape.

00:03:45.273 --> 00:03:49.894
Combs, scissors and clippers are cleaned and disinfected after every client.

00:03:50.149 --> 00:03:51.494
For lash extensions:

00:03:51.763 --> 00:03:55.163
tweezers are cleaned and disinfected after every client,

00:03:55.113 --> 00:03:58.214
and lash wands and cotton swabs are used only once.

00:03:58.476 --> 00:03:59.494
For pedicures:

00:03:59.762 --> 00:04:02.119
line the foot bath with a disposable liner,

00:04:02.069 --> 00:04:04.694
and keep the pedicure tools apart from the rest.

00:04:04.856 --> 00:04:09.174
When doing acrylic nails, you must have dust extraction right at the table.

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:11.897
If you accidentally make a client bleed:

00:04:12.003 --> 00:04:17.737
stop, put on new gloves, clean the wound, disinfect it, and cover it with a plaster.

00:04:18.396 --> 00:04:21.258
A surface with blood on it must always be disinfected,

00:04:21.208 --> 00:04:23.497
and that tool goes straight for processing,

00:04:23.528 --> 00:04:24.697
not back into use.

00:04:25.038 --> 00:04:29.286
And if you see signs of infection on the skin or nails, politely decline,

00:04:29.236 --> 00:04:31.817
and advise the client to see a doctor first.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.232
Finally, the regulations.

00:04:34.576 --> 00:04:38.072
Every country, and every city, has its own requirements.

00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:39.855
In Finland, for example,

00:04:39.805 --> 00:04:47.912
most beauty salons that offer skin treatments must notify the health protection authority of the city at least thirty days before opening,

00:04:48.181 --> 00:04:50.712
and must have an in-house hygiene control plan.

00:04:51.141 --> 00:04:53.912
Ask the health authority where you work, so you get it right.

00:04:54.482 --> 00:04:57.752
Cleanliness is the best advertisement a salon can have.

00:04:57.922 --> 00:05:00.792
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
